        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/h/cc9497/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2018-04-06T07:33:45.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Handelabra previewed the Tribunal last tuesday.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Using the power from the representative works exactly like 'I can do that too' from Guise's deck.</p><p>The hero use the power the representative has : With Nightmist as representative, one hero can draw 2 cards and deals himself 2 damage.</p><p>If Chrono Ranger use tiny Extremist Sky-Sky power, he can boost the damage with his bounty and 'hunted and hunting'.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The thing that surprised me, is that if you play with a hero, you can still choose one of this hero's variant as a representative.</p><p>So if you play Guise, you can use Completionnist Guise as representative then allow Guise to switch himself as Santa Guise ... which from a story point of view should make the Tribunal explose from sheer nonsense.</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:47:13.562Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
